/-!
# Pinned local target: correlated exponent 4/5 (depth-8 shared lift)

Depth-8 analogue of `BackwardThreeQuarters`.  Source residues run modulo
`19683 = 3^9`, child residues modulo `6561 = 3^8`, over the same five height
floors `{1, 7/4, 3, 6, 12}` (whose geometry is reused verbatim from the
three-quarter module).  The frozen `21870`-entry potential and the `65610`
source-state/lift inequalities are exactly those produced by
`experiments/barrier_transfer.py --correlated-four-fifths-certificate`.

The rational edge underweight is `(75257/31250)·(574349/1000000)^j`, valid for
exponent `4/5` because `(75257/31250)^5 < 81` and `16·(574349/1000000)^5 < 1`.
-/

namespace CollatzMoonshot.FrontA

/-! ## Frozen 21870-state potential (five floors x 4374 unit residues mod 6561)

Order: height state outermost, then the 4374 positive unit residues modulo 6561
in increasing order.  For a unit residue `r = 3q+1` its zero-based index is `2q`;
for `r = 3q+2` it is `2q+1` (`fourFifthsUnitIndex`, identical formula to the
three-quarter module).
-/

